{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>What is this that Elohim has done to us.</b> That He put it in this one's heart — despite his being a God-fearer — to do this to us, in order to subdue us as slaves when we come to him. As they said afterward (Genesis 43:18): וְלָקַחַת אוֹתָנוּ לַעֲבָדִים ('and take us as slaves'). And this is to repay us measure for measure for the selling of our brother. Now the selling was not done by us with intent to harm, but because we considered him a pursuer liable to the death penalty; and that we did not kill him was an act of mercy, since he was our brother."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:21.784423373Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}